<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM keeps mum on likely new partners.</title>
<headline>KLM keeps mum on likely new partners.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch carrier KLM said on Wednesday it would seek to widen its reinforced alliance with U.S. partner Northwest with new partners, but stayed tight-lipped on likely candidates.</p>
<p>&quot;The two partners (KLM and Northwest) will pursue further widening of their alliance with new partners,&quot; KLM said in a statement announcing the sale of its 19 percent Northwest stake.</p>
<p>But an airline spokesman declined to name any prospective partners. &quot;We do not comment until there is something firm to report,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
